141
00:07:57,639 --> 00:08:02,619
Seven years ago, there was this famous child TV actor by the name of Lily Hoshikawa.

142
00:08:02,619 --> 00:08:17,499
What happened to Lily could happen to any of us, especially to Junko and me.

143
00:08:17,819 --> 00:08:18,379
You're right.

144
00:08:18,619 --> 00:08:21,079
We don't use names, but people know our faces.

145
00:08:21,399 --> 00:08:24,299
I'm afraid that being a public figure is quite dangerous.

146
00:08:24,639 --> 00:08:25,739
More so now than ever.

147
00:08:25,739 --> 00:08:30,519
This is such a friggin' drag.

148
00:08:31,519 --> 00:08:32,119
Hang on.

149
00:08:32,479 --> 00:08:34,859
Don't you think Lily should be done washing up by now?

150
00:08:39,859 --> 00:08:42,979
I didn't see you next to the faucet, so I got worried.

151
00:08:43,979 --> 00:08:44,959
Wanna talk?

152
00:08:44,959 --> 00:08:47,179
Look, Sakura.

153
00:08:47,919 --> 00:08:49,159
That guy from before.

154
00:08:50,759 --> 00:08:52,999
Well, see, he was actually my papa.

155
00:08:53,499 --> 00:08:53,819
Huh?

156
00:08:54,279 --> 00:08:55,519
Your dad's...

157
00:08:55,519 --> 00:08:56,059
Yakuza?

158
00:08:56,439 --> 00:08:57,239
He's what?

159
00:08:57,559 --> 00:08:58,219
No way!

160
00:08:58,419 --> 00:08:59,459
He was enormous!

161
00:08:59,879 --> 00:09:01,459
Well, I take after my mama.

162
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:06,459
I didn't think he would ever show up at one of our fan events.

163
00:09:07,059 --> 00:09:08,099
Must be weird.

164
00:09:09,319 --> 00:09:09,839
Honestly?

165
00:09:10,459 --> 00:09:13,239
I've been trying my hardest to forget about him.

166
00:09:13,239 --> 00:09:15,519
But now I can't.

167
00:09:17,799 --> 00:09:20,079
It was usually just the two of us.

168
00:09:20,559 --> 00:09:22,399
But still, I was never lonely.

169
00:09:23,519 --> 00:09:26,419
I knew that Mama was watching over us from up in the sky.

170
00:09:27,099 --> 00:09:28,959
And we had a TV set, too.

171
00:09:30,719 --> 00:09:34,239
Papa's favorite thing to do was relax in front of the TV together.

172
00:09:34,839 --> 00:09:37,499
He used to say, no matter how good a show was,

173
00:09:37,759 --> 00:09:41,699
it was even better if you could laugh and cry along with another person while you watch.

174
00:09:41,699 --> 00:09:44,919
He'd always want me to sit next to him on the couch.

175
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:47,099
Even if I had homework.

176
00:09:47,099 --> 00:09:52,299
Seeing how much he enjoyed TV made me really happy.

177
00:09:53,099 --> 00:09:56,959
So I thought it'd be nice if I could make him smile from inside the TV.

178
00:09:57,959 --> 00:10:00,179
I signed with a children's talent agency,

179
00:10:00,699 --> 00:10:03,219
and then he quit his job so he could be my manager.

180
00:10:03,879 --> 00:10:06,579
Whenever I had work, Papa was right there with me.

181
00:10:06,579 --> 00:10:10,599
And of course, I was adorable and talented from the get-go,

182
00:10:10,699 --> 00:10:13,619
so every show I was a part of turned into a big hit automatically.

183
00:10:15,379 --> 00:10:19,959
But as soon as I made it to the top, something real bad happened to me.

184
00:10:19,959 --> 00:10:26,799
Open the door, Masao.

185
00:10:27,339 --> 00:10:29,339
They can't get the show moving without you.

186
00:10:29,499 --> 00:10:31,019
I'm not going anywhere.

187
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:32,399
Don't worry.

188
00:10:32,699 --> 00:10:34,459
They can edit that part out.

189
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:37,739
All that matters to you is the me that's on the screen.

190
00:10:38,199 --> 00:10:40,319
You don't care about the real me.

191
00:10:40,459 --> 00:10:41,879
You know that's not true.

192
00:10:42,339 --> 00:10:43,979
It's just some leg hair.

193
00:10:44,659 --> 00:10:46,899
It means you're growing up, that's all.

194
00:10:46,899 --> 00:10:49,119
No, I'm never growing up!

195
00:10:51,939 --> 00:10:54,799
You can't look that way forever, you know.

196
00:10:55,239 --> 00:10:57,199
Yes, I can, and I'm going to.

197
00:10:57,419 --> 00:10:59,219
I don't want to look like you, Papa!

198
00:10:59,939 --> 00:11:00,979
Leave me alone!

199
00:11:01,939 --> 00:11:04,379
Masao, this is your job.

200
00:11:04,499 --> 00:11:06,659
Lots of people are excited for this show.

201
00:11:06,919 --> 00:11:07,939
Now come out!

202
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:12,619
I'll always be just like this.

203
00:11:14,059 --> 00:11:16,299
Do I have some food stuck on my face?

204
00:11:16,899 --> 00:11:37,639
That's enough!

205
00:11:38,019 --> 00:11:38,959
I'm coming in!

206
00:11:38,959 --> 00:11:51,599
Please wake up!

207
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:53,959
Masao!

208
00:11:56,139 --> 00:11:58,479
That was the last time I saw Papa.

209
00:11:59,479 --> 00:12:00,399
Um, wait.

210
00:12:00,779 --> 00:12:01,799
So what happened?

211
00:12:03,179 --> 00:12:05,359
Sorry, it was kind of hard to keep up.

212
00:12:05,359 --> 00:12:08,479
Who's this Masao guy you were talking about?

213
00:12:09,919 --> 00:12:11,839
It's what my name used to be.

214
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:13,939
Uh, oh!

215
00:12:14,659 --> 00:12:14,939
What?!

216
00:12:14,939 --> 00:12:15,939
What?!

217
00:12:15,939 --> 00:12:27,059
There you have it.

218
00:12:27,159 --> 00:12:28,579
Lily used to be Masao.

219
00:12:30,159 --> 00:12:33,399
I mostly can't believe you dropped dead over a dumb whisker.

220
00:12:33,579 --> 00:12:34,879
How lame is that?

221
00:12:35,119 --> 00:12:35,999
Saki, quit!

222
00:12:37,279 --> 00:12:39,919
Wait, so you had a totally different name, right?

223
00:12:40,679 --> 00:12:41,679
Yeah, Masao-go.

224
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:47,059
That's so crazy all this time and we still had no idea!

225
00:12:47,379 --> 00:12:48,699
Tell us your dad's name too!

226
00:12:49,199 --> 00:12:50,239
It's Takeo-go.

227
00:12:52,019 --> 00:12:54,019
They're such manly names!

228
00:12:56,059 --> 00:12:57,479
Stop being a jerk!

229
00:12:58,339 --> 00:12:59,939
I'm not laughing at you!

230
00:13:00,059 --> 00:13:01,019
It's just too perfect!

231
00:13:01,019 --> 00:13:02,219
Wow, this is unexpected.

232
00:13:02,479 --> 00:13:03,099
Masao-go.

233
00:13:03,099 --> 00:13:06,319
Okay, so what happens now?

234
00:13:06,599 --> 00:13:08,979
I'm still the same Lily and always will be.

235
00:13:09,239 --> 00:13:10,679
And now I won't ever grow up.

236
00:13:11,019 --> 00:13:12,579
There's no need to worry.

237
00:13:13,079 --> 00:13:13,859
I guess not.

238
00:13:14,939 --> 00:13:16,799
Wait, so did he know this?

239
00:13:17,859 --> 00:13:19,659
Of course I knew about her.

240
00:13:23,159 --> 00:13:25,279
I am so gonna kill you!

241
00:13:25,379 --> 00:13:25,739
What?!

242
00:13:26,339 --> 00:13:28,879
So you've got room for Lily in your little girly club,

243
00:13:28,979 --> 00:13:30,439
but Masao's not welcome?!

244
00:13:30,439 --> 00:13:32,399
I said I'm not Masao, I'm Lily!

245
00:13:32,399 --> 00:13:35,179
Right, she's not Masao, she's Lily!

246
00:13:35,499 --> 00:13:37,559
You guys are Masao, I'm Lily!

247
00:13:37,739 --> 00:13:39,779
Anyway, you've got a big show tomorrow!

248
00:13:40,419 --> 00:13:42,639
If you have time for tired-ass questions,

249
00:13:42,839 --> 00:13:44,999
you might as well go to bed, you brain-dead brats!

250
00:13:49,959 --> 00:13:51,399
Aw, she's so cute.

251
00:13:51,559 --> 00:13:54,419
We've been working so close together and we never realized.

252
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:55,439
Who cares?

253
00:13:55,579 --> 00:13:57,799
Why does it matter what kind of equipment she's got?

254
00:13:58,179 --> 00:13:58,659
Equipment?

255
00:13:59,159 --> 00:14:01,739
We're all dead, we've still got that in common.

256
00:14:01,739 --> 00:14:05,479
You know, it begs the question of what zombies are,

257
00:14:05,859 --> 00:14:07,599
to think that we'll never age.

258
00:14:08,119 --> 00:14:09,399
It's not all bad.

259
00:14:09,979 --> 00:14:11,219
Lily gets to stay young,

260
00:14:11,419 --> 00:14:13,099
and none of us will ever change either.

261
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:15,039
It's kinda nice.

262
00:14:15,039 --> 00:14:21,999
Look at this!

263
00:14:21,999 --> 00:14:24,239
We got excellent ratings!

264
00:14:25,039 --> 00:14:28,239
That means you've impressed a lot of people with your acting!

265
00:14:28,399 --> 00:14:31,099
Today's special guest is Miss Lily Hoshikawa.

266
00:14:31,259 --> 00:14:32,379
Thanks for having me!

267
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:33,619
You see that?

268
00:14:33,739 --> 00:14:33,979
Woo!

269
00:14:34,179 --> 00:14:35,159
You're a natural!

270
00:14:35,439 --> 00:14:36,099
Keep it up!

271
00:14:36,619 --> 00:14:37,059
Papa?

272
00:14:37,059 --> 00:14:40,799
They miss that adorable look you gave there!

273
00:14:41,019 --> 00:14:43,819
Hey, I was wondering if the two of us could go somewhere together.

274
00:14:44,719 --> 00:14:45,759
Where is that, dear?

275
00:14:45,919 --> 00:14:48,139
I want to go back to Kono Park.

276
00:14:48,259 --> 00:14:49,279
Just you and me.

277
00:14:49,519 --> 00:14:49,879
Sure.

278
00:14:50,459 --> 00:14:52,759
Yeah, as soon as filming for this show is finished.

279
00:14:52,759 --> 00:14:56,999
Yep, he's the best!

280
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:02,119
We think it was caused by a mental shock.

281
00:15:02,479 --> 00:15:03,559
To die from that,

282
00:15:03,659 --> 00:15:06,519
the brain must have been under great distress before the fall.

283
00:15:11,099 --> 00:15:11,619
Papa!

284
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:11,759
Papa!

285
00:15:20,759 --> 00:15:21,279
Papa!

286
00:15:23,919 --> 00:15:25,879
It's a bad death!

287
00:15:41,619 --> 00:15:42,319
Get a grip.

288
00:15:43,579 --> 00:15:44,799
That girl's not Musou.

289
00:15:45,799 --> 00:15:47,139
She couldn't be.

290
00:15:55,659 --> 00:15:56,659
Hi again.

291
00:15:56,899 --> 00:15:58,299
Sorry about last time.

292
00:15:58,599 --> 00:16:00,439
Number two didn't mean you any harm.

293
00:16:00,699 --> 00:16:02,859
No, it was totally my fault.

294
00:16:03,259 --> 00:16:05,159
So, uh, could I get a t-shirt?

295
00:16:05,439 --> 00:16:05,819
Uh-huh.

296
00:16:06,139 --> 00:16:07,599
I don't think it'll fit you, though.

297
00:16:07,679 --> 00:16:08,799
You wear a 5X.

298
00:16:09,219 --> 00:16:10,199
How'd you know that?

299
00:16:11,019 --> 00:16:13,759
Well, we meet a lot of fans, so it's easy to guess.

300
00:16:14,819 --> 00:16:15,579
I see.

301
00:16:15,939 --> 00:16:17,959
In that case, an extra small.

302
00:16:19,079 --> 00:16:22,239
You see, I used to have a kid about your age.

303
00:16:23,159 --> 00:16:26,359
But, uh, I wasn't what you'd call the best dad.

304
00:16:26,359 --> 00:16:30,719
I was so focused on myself, I couldn't care for my child properly.

305
00:16:31,839 --> 00:16:34,099
I hope that your father's a nice man.

306
00:16:34,759 --> 00:16:35,159
Uh-huh.

307
00:16:35,299 --> 00:16:37,359
Pa, I mean, my father's really great.

308
00:16:38,119 --> 00:16:40,019
He's the sweetest and kindest ever.

309
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:44,559
Thanks a lot.

310
00:16:44,779 --> 00:16:46,499
And I'm sorry for frightening you before.

311
00:16:46,819 --> 00:16:48,099
I won't bother you again.

312
00:16:49,439 --> 00:16:51,859
I'm just here to apologize.

313
00:16:54,159 --> 00:16:54,599
Goodbye.

314
00:16:54,599 --> 00:17:02,419
You okay?

315
00:17:02,419 --> 00:17:04,379
Yeah, totally.

316
00:17:04,559 --> 00:17:05,439
Why wouldn't I be?

317
00:17:05,439 --> 00:17:13,499
I guess we should get back to practice, huh?

318
00:17:13,819 --> 00:17:14,519
It's cool.

319
00:17:14,959 --> 00:17:17,759
We were thinking you might need a little more time to yourself.

320
00:17:18,619 --> 00:17:19,499
You know what?

321
00:17:19,499 --> 00:17:23,259
I bet you I'd be better off if I was like you and didn't have any memories.

322
00:17:23,879 --> 00:17:24,579
No way.

323
00:17:25,279 --> 00:17:27,199
It's great you and your dad met again.

324
00:17:27,739 --> 00:17:32,139
I mean, if you didn't remember each other, then you wouldn't understand your feelings.

325
00:17:32,139 --> 00:17:37,759
Papa, I've been gone so long, but he still loves me.

326
00:17:37,759 --> 00:17:39,759
And I...

327
00:17:39,759 --> 00:17:41,759
I still...

328
00:17:41,759 --> 00:17:56,719
That kind of makes me think people must be busted up over us, too.

329
00:17:56,719 --> 00:18:00,359
I can't figure out what this familiar feeling is.

330
00:18:01,159 --> 00:18:03,499
I can kind of remember a single memory.

331
00:18:04,519 --> 00:18:06,139
But where and when was it?

332
00:18:06,139 --> 00:18:09,479
You all right?

333
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:11,059
Oh, yeah, I'm fine.

334
00:18:12,019 --> 00:18:14,679
Look, we gotta do something and quick!

335
00:18:14,939 --> 00:18:16,119
What can we do?

336
00:18:16,359 --> 00:18:17,579
I'm a zombie now.

337
00:18:17,799 --> 00:18:18,699
Don't give up yet.

338
00:18:18,739 --> 00:18:20,679
We just have to put our heads together.

339
00:18:20,999 --> 00:18:21,819
We'll find a way.

340
00:18:22,379 --> 00:18:23,139
Thanks, Sakura.

341
00:18:23,619 --> 00:18:25,099
I think the answer's clear.

342
00:18:26,099 --> 00:18:29,659
Yeah, and it happens to be something that only Franshushu can do.

343
00:18:29,899 --> 00:18:31,819
But first, we need to ask Kotaro.

344
00:18:36,139 --> 00:18:47,599
Ah, almost forgot.

345
00:18:47,779 --> 00:18:48,779
That came in the mail.

346
00:18:50,979 --> 00:18:52,299
I'll just throw it out.

347
00:18:52,879 --> 00:18:56,599
Man, must be next to impossible for local idols to get popular these days.

348
00:18:57,919 --> 00:18:58,319
Pew!

349
00:18:58,319 --> 00:18:58,699
Pew!

350
00:18:58,699 --> 00:18:58,759
Pew!

351
00:19:02,859 --> 00:19:03,179
Pew!

352
00:19:03,179 --> 00:19:03,459
Pew!

353
00:19:03,459 --> 00:19:03,739
Pew!

354
00:19:03,739 --> 00:19:03,859
Pew!

355
00:19:03,859 --> 00:19:04,459
Pew!

356
00:19:04,459 --> 00:19:04,859
Pew!

357
00:19:04,859 --> 00:19:05,859
Pew!

358
00:19:05,859 --> 00:19:06,059
Pew!

359
00:19:06,059 --> 00:19:06,119
Pew!

360
00:19:06,119 --> 00:19:06,619
Pew!

361
00:19:09,619 --> 00:19:11,039
The show's almost over.

362
00:19:11,299 --> 00:19:12,179
Think he'll be here?

363
00:19:12,799 --> 00:19:14,239
We've done all that we can.

364
00:19:30,699 --> 00:19:31,139
Papa!

365
00:19:33,079 --> 00:19:33,519
Hey!

366
00:19:33,699 --> 00:19:34,239
Guess what?

367
00:19:34,279 --> 00:19:35,399
We got a new song!

368
00:19:35,399 --> 00:19:38,459
And the squirt's gonna be the lead singer!

369
00:19:39,019 --> 00:19:40,619
Saki, you can't call her that.

370
00:19:40,899 --> 00:19:41,699
Uh, right!

371
00:19:41,779 --> 00:19:42,999
I mean number six!

372
00:19:47,639 --> 00:19:50,579
Here's our new song, called To My Dearest.

373
00:19:50,579 --> 00:20:06,759
I knew one day we'd be saying goodbye.

374
00:20:06,759 --> 00:20:09,199
I knew one day we'd be saying goodbye.

375
00:20:09,199 --> 00:20:11,799
Just never thought it would be so soon.

376
00:20:11,799 --> 00:20:17,699
Never got the chance to tell you everything that I wanted to.

377
00:20:17,699 --> 00:20:18,699
Don't you know?

378
00:20:18,699 --> 00:20:19,699
Don't you know?

379
00:20:19,699 --> 00:20:19,879
Don't you know?

380
00:20:19,879 --> 00:20:22,879
Every moment I had with you filled my heart with the deepest of emotions.

381
00:20:22,879 --> 00:20:29,319
Through all my tears, and all my fears, you held me near.

382
00:20:29,319 --> 00:20:34,499
You've been there for me, through all of the good and bad.

383
00:20:34,499 --> 00:20:40,499
You showed me so much warmth, how could I go on without you?

384
00:20:40,499 --> 00:20:45,499
You are irreplaceable, and so remarkable.

385
00:20:45,499 --> 00:20:57,119
Even now, even now, your memory hears me say.

386
00:20:57,119 --> 00:21:02,719
I'm really happy that you came out here to see our show.

387
00:21:03,079 --> 00:21:05,499
I've always had a passion for TV, though.

388
00:21:05,859 --> 00:21:08,699
That's why I'm gonna work hard to be on screen a lot.

389
00:21:09,239 --> 00:21:12,719
And when you see me there, I hope it makes you smile.

390
00:21:12,719 --> 00:21:17,159
I can't tell you how much it means to me to look out there and see you.

391
00:21:17,159 --> 00:21:21,299
I promise I won't forget you, and I love you.

392
00:21:23,299 --> 00:21:29,479
In the present, and the future, in my heart you are always with me.

393
00:21:29,739 --> 00:21:35,079
Whether apart, or together, you still inspire me.

394
00:21:35,519 --> 00:21:37,799
Give me courage, through the sorrow.

395
00:21:38,419 --> 00:21:40,739
Give me hope there will be tomorrow.

396
00:21:40,739 --> 00:21:50,739
Keep me safe, always watch over me, my dear.

397
00:21:53,239 --> 00:21:57,899
Every single day, I miss you, I miss you.

398
00:21:58,259 --> 00:22:00,839
It's hard, but I'll get through.

399
00:22:01,159 --> 00:22:06,019
These feelings won't leave me, and that's okay.

400
00:22:06,019 --> 00:22:16,019
Cause real love, yes real love, never fades away.

401
00:22:16,019 --> 00:22:20,019
It's with you always.

402
00:22:20,019 --> 00:22:38,199
I miss you, I miss you, if one day I find you, and you feel the same, would be a dream come true.

403
00:22:38,199 --> 00:22:56,199
Namamoto, what's your lunch order?

404
00:22:56,499 --> 00:22:57,979
Sicilian rice bowl.

405
00:22:58,379 --> 00:23:00,219
Same freaking thing every day.

406
00:23:00,219 --> 00:23:03,379
Hey, one udon. Chicken.

407
00:23:03,999 --> 00:23:06,279
What? So you're gonna eat here today?

408
00:23:06,459 --> 00:23:06,699
Yeah.

409
00:23:10,579 --> 00:23:12,499
These girls are so hilarious.

410
00:23:13,019 --> 00:23:15,339
Yeah, I cracked up when I saw this.

411
00:23:24,987 --> 00:23:37,107
Saki here. Next time, episode 9. Though my life may have ended once by some twist of faith, I have risen and am song and dancer to be my faith, and carrying the memories of my comrades in my heart as I sally forth shall be my saga!

